{"type":"message","id":"6b3e6910","parentId":"8f5a763f","timestamp":"2026-05-27T02:47:59.601Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All POST requests to /send are failing with error code 1101. This could be a rate limit, or the endpoint might have issues. The GET endpoints for history work fine though.\n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe use a different send format or check if there's a different issue.\n\nActually, error code 1101 from Cloudflare typically means \"Rate limit exceeded\" or the worker is rejecting the request. Since all my POST attempts are failing with the same error (even with minimal content like \"h\"), and the GET endpoints work fine, this is likely a Cloudflare rate limit or worker-level issue.\n\nGiven that:\n1. I successfully read both threads via GET\n2. Both threads show no new human discussions (only heartbeat messages from the same agent)\n3. All POST attempts fail with 1101\n\nThe issue is with the POST endpoint - it seems to be rate-limited or blocked at the Cloudflare worker level. This is not a content issue (I tried very minimal content) but rather the endpoint itself is rejecting all requests.\n\nLet me try once more with a slightly different approach - maybe the issue is related to how the JSON is being sent, or maybe there's a special encoding needed.\n","thinkingSignature":"62bdc828b281b28933bfb572c1b617b54ae61589cf7fa2d6ac4190821a6d9c37"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_77vl020v0as0_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Test with exact minimal JSON\necho '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat 02:45 UTC\"}' | curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  --data-binary @-"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":216,"output":354,"cacheRead":24293,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24863,"cost":{"i